{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-277834-r4615132","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Peach Chutney","sourcePageId":277834,"sourceRevision":"4615132","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-02-03T02:22:28Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Peach%20Chutney&oldid=4615132","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:20:13.786Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for chutney","Category:Recipes for curry","Category:Recipes using asafoetida","Category:Recipes using brown sugar","Category:Recipes using celery seed","Category:Recipes using fresh ginger","Category:Recipes using garam masala","Category:Recipes using lemon juice","Category:Recipes using mustard seed","Category:Recipes using peach","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"203e33434b03cdc78dfd99755624657b8f2611a07abd43e23c7ac7397b1d7032","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Chutney recipes\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} \n\nThis is great served with [[Cookbook:Pork|pork]] chops or curry.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n* 6 ½ [[Cookbook:Pound|pounds]] [[Cookbook:Peach|peaches]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] dark [[Cookbook:Raisin|raisins]]\n* 2 cup [[Cookbook:Lemon Juice|lemon juice]]\n* 1 cup golden raisins\n* 2 cup [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] pickling salt\n* ¾ cup finely [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]]\n* 1 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Mustard|mustard]] seed\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Asafoetida|asafoetida]]\n* 2 tablespoon [[Cookbook:Celery Seed|celery seed]]\n* 1 hot [[Cookbook:Banana pepper|banana pepper]], seeded and chopped\n* 2 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Garam Masala|garam masala]] (curry blend) \n* 2 green peppers, finely chopped\n\n== Procedure ==\n#[[Cookbook:Blanching|Blanch]], peel, and pit peaches. \n#Coarsely chop peaches and combine with lemon juice in a large stainless steel or enamel [[Cookbook:Saucepan|saucepan]]. Stir in sugar. \n#Bring to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]] and cook, stirring frequently until the peaches are tender (about 15 minutes). \n#Add remaining ingredients. Boil over medium-high heat for about 45 minutes or until thick, stirring frequently. \n#Ladle chutney into six hot, sterilized, 1-pint (2-cup) preserving jars, leaving ½ inch of headspace. Wipe rims clean and seal according to manufacturer's directions.\n#Process for 15 minutes in a boiling water bath. Allow chutney to mature for at least one month before using.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using peach]]\n[[Category:Recipes for chutney]]\n[[Category:Recipes for curry]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using asafoetida]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery seed]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lemon juice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garam masala]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fresh ginger]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mustard seed]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Peach Chutney","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"6 ½ pounds peaches","sourceText":"6 ½ pounds peaches","amountText":"6 ½ pounds peaches","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 cup dark raisins","sourceText":"1 cup dark raisins","amountText":"1 cup dark raisins","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"2 cup lemon juice","sourceText":"2 cup lemon juice","amountText":"2 cup lemon juice","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 cup golden raisins","sourceText":"1 cup golden raisins","amountText":"1 cup golden raisins","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"2 cup brown sugar","sourceText":"2 cup brown sugar","amountText":"2 cup brown sugar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1 tablespoon pickling salt","sourceText":"1 tablespoon pickling salt","amountText":"1 tablespoon pickling salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"¾ cup finely chopped ginger","sourceText":"¾ cup finely chopped ginger","amountText":"¾ cup finely chopped ginger","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"1 tablespoon mustard seed","sourceText":"1 tablespoon mustard seed","amountText":"1 tablespoon mustard seed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"1 teaspoon asafoetida","sourceText":"1 teaspoon asafoetida","amountText":"1 teaspoon asafoetida","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-10","name":"2 tablespoon celery seed","sourceText":"2 tablespoon celery seed","amountText":"2 tablespoon celery seed","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-11","name":"1 hot banana pepper, seeded and chopped","sourceText":"1 hot banana pepper, seeded and chopped","amountText":"1 hot banana pepper, seeded and chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-12","name":"2 teaspoon garam masala (curry blend)","sourceText":"2 teaspoon garam masala (curry blend)","amountT